# CODEOWNERS — the owner-gated surfaces (PRD 7.5, rule R-H).
#
# Agents merge their own work when CI is green EXCEPT on these paths, where a
# mistake is expensive or irreversible: settled architecture, what ships in the
# image, the privilege boundary, and the pipeline that reaches users' machines.
#
# ARMED. All three preconditions are satisfied and verified:
#
#   [x] Repo is public, so branch protection is available on the free plan.
#   [x] Branch protection on `main`: lint + build-x86_64 + build-aarch64 must
#       pass, code-owner review required, 1 approval, stale reviews dismissed,
#       linear history, no force pushes or deletions. Admins may bypass, because
#       GitHub forbids self-approval and full enforcement would deadlock a solo
#       owner's own pull requests.
#   [x] The `owners` team has write access, so every rule below resolves.
#
# That last one is the fragile part and it fails SILENTLY: GitHub applies no
# review requirement at all for an unresolvable owner, and the file still reads
# like a gate. The lint workflow therefore asks GitHub directly on every run:
#
#   gh api 'repos/{owner}/{repo}/codeowners/errors'   -> must be empty
#
# Check that first if a rule here ever appears not to be doing its job.

# Settled law. Changing an ADR is an owner decision, never an agent's (PRD 0.1).
/docs/adr/                  @ReclaimExperience/owners
/docs/PRD.md                @ReclaimExperience/owners

# What ships in the image. Removals in particular can silently break drivers.
/os/packages.yml            @ReclaimExperience/owners

# The privilege boundary (ADR-015). Three custom polkit actions exist in total.
/os/rootfs/etc/polkit-1/        @ReclaimExperience/owners  # planned: WP-12
/os/rootfs/usr/share/polkit-1/  @ReclaimExperience/owners  # planned: WP-12
/docs/security-notes.md         @ReclaimExperience/owners  # planned: WP-13

# The pipeline that reaches users' machines, and image signing policy (ADR-014).
/ci/                                        @ReclaimExperience/owners
/.github/workflows/                         @ReclaimExperience/owners
/os/rootfs/etc/containers/policy.json       @ReclaimExperience/owners  # planned: WP-04

# The gates themselves. Rule R-E: budgets are laws; you never edit the gate.
# The harness IS a gate. An agent could not widen allowed-ports.txt without
# review, but could weaken is_local(), delete an assertion, or paste a
# full-image mask into a baseline config with none — a bigger hole than the one
# the allowlists close.
/tests/harness/             @ReclaimExperience/owners
/tests/baselines/           @ReclaimExperience/owners
/tests/stories/             @ReclaimExperience/owners

/tests/lint/                @ReclaimExperience/owners
/tests/perf/                @ReclaimExperience/owners
/tests/privacy/             @ReclaimExperience/owners
/tests/security/            @ReclaimExperience/owners
